ull,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105072","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105072","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105072.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105072.patch","merged_at":"2025-04-07T13:46:47Z"},"body":"Currently, the minimum size of GUI items in the OpenXR module is constant. This means for devices with differing editor scales (`Godot -> Editor Settings -> Interface -> Editor -> Display Scale`) the GUI can be too small or too big, as the total number of pixels does not scale, but elements like the font do. This PR brings the OpenXR module in alignment with many of the other editor GUI elements by scaling the size of GUI elements according to the current `editor scale`.\r\n\r\nGodot 4.4 (with 2x scale), note the cut-off text:\r\n<img width=\"920\" alt=\"Before the PR (2x scale)\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/eb9a2864-b778-4cbd-9849-667185a427d4\" />\r\n\r\nThis PR (with 2x scale):\r\n<img width=\"926\" alt=\"After the PR (2x scale)\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ef545396-9ff8-4d21-81d2-d8d3c17ef315\" />","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","r